==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Sakura Matou CC''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Dark Sakura CC''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Because of her health, range and [[Resistant|resistance]], Sakura Matou can be used as a mid-ranged tank against enemies in her target traits your meatshields can't handle. She also has the [[Zombie Killer]] ability which makes her even more effective against zombies.

Better yet, she's immune to [[Wave Attack|waves]], making her useful against such enemies due to her medium range. Notably, this can work on [[Multiversal Studios]] (zombies backed by [[Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Doge Base]]) and makes dealing with enemies like [[Elizabeth the LVIth|Elizabeth]]/[[Two Can]]/[[Axoloty]]/[[Youcan]] even easier.

Here are some stages where she's very effective:
*[[Hearts of Darkness (Merciless)|Hearts of Darkness]] (Growing Strange), against [[Razorback]], [[Shadow Boxer K]] and [[Tackey]] (fits inside his blindspot) with [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]]
*[[Moon (Into the Future)|Into the Future, Moon stages]] against [[Cli-One]], [[Corrupted Valkyrie]] and [[Raging Bahamut Cat|Raging Bahamut]]
*[[Parade of the Dead (Deadly)|Dead on Debut]], against [[Daboo of the Dead|Daboo]] (beware of the Angels and Daboo's slow ability)
*[[Seas of Death (Merciless)|Seas of Death]], against [[Zamelle]]
*[[Multiversal Studios]], overall fantastic against not only the Doge Base for Wave Immunity, but also can tank several devastating hits from [[Inumusha]] for a long time, granted you use meatshields to protect her from Zories.

==='''True Form'''===
Dark Sakura CC gains a couple of abilities to further augment her potential on the field. The attack rate bonus is minor, but does allow her to catch enemies more often and finish off zombies earlier. Soulstrike is essential for eliminating zombies before they revive, also allowing her to stay behind and keep them occupied if she fails to destroy them outright. Freeze Immunity isn't as useful, since such enemies are few and far between in her traits, although it does serve helpful against [[Zir Zeal]], [[Death Angel Z-Onel]] (if you have a solution for those aliens, as she is not warp immune), [[Maawth]], [[I.M. Phace]] and [[Bakoo]], and can also help in getting around [[Henry]] if he backs said enemies, such as in [[Virtual Nightmare]]. With a relatively low cost as well (only the usual 1,000,000 EXP and 3 Epic Fruits), this True Form is definitely worth getting if you struggle against such enemies.

==='''Talents'''===
The flashiest Talent here is '''[[Weaken]]''', doubling her effective HP against targets if it activates. At a 50% activation rate, it is beyond janky for the NP it asks of you. While the uptime is great, Sakura's attack rate is quite sluggish, and if it doesn't activate on the enemies you want it to, you have to wait a grueling 6 seconds to try again.

'''[[Immune to Toxic]]''' enables two specific matchups: [[Zollow]] and [[Casaurian Darkjo]]. She's a great counter to the former, whose purpose is typically to disrupt your meatshield flow and delete any tanks he comes across. Sakura can continue to tank her targets while completely disregarding his presence, usually killing him in the process. Darkjo is always accompanied by dangerous non-target peons that will rip her to shreds if given the chance. If you protect her well, she can tank him just fine, but be wary of the circumstances just as much as the enemy itself.

Just like every other Talent of its kind, '''[[Special Abilities#Resist|Resist Curse]]''' is borderline worthless. It gives Sakura slightly better survivability in specific Uncanny Legends stages with enemies like [[Loris]], or in cases where a stray [[Sir Rel]] hits her, but these scenarios are extremely uncommon. [[Endless Forms Most Beautiful]] is the most notable stage where this Talent is of use, but even there she struggles against the high-magnification enemies.

'''Defense Buff''' is always good to have since she's a tanker, but be sure to boost her with [[Catseye]]s first. '''Attack Buff''' is sacrilege.

==='''Orb'''===
For Effect Orbs, a Dark/Alien/Zombie Resistant Orb are the most beneficial, as they give Dark Sakura extra health against specific target traits. Otherwise, Defense Orbs against the aforementioned traits will suffice.

For Ability Orbs, an A-Rank Resist Curse Orb would effectively give Dark Sakura full '''Curse Immunity'''. However, it ends up being completely useless due to her not targeting Relics, resulting in very few viable matchups in mixed stages.

